|rarity = SR
|name1 = Kotomine & Gilgamesh Cats
|name2 = Gilgamesh & Kotomine Cats
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gilgamesh & Kotomine Cats''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Kotomine & Gilgamesh Cats resemble [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Catophone]] in stats, though the former have a few perks that make them more appealing, albeit slightly. Their Strengthen allows them to reach 3,632.4 DPS, exceeding that of Catophone and even [[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Tathagata Cat]]. This would make them quite appealing if their recharge time wasn't massive. Since Kotomine & Gilgamesh Cats can't be spammed, other units like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] are much better offensively due to having a much more tolerable cooldown and thus being able to be stacked faster.

Using Kotomine & Gilgamesh Cats as crowd-control isn't any better. While two of them are enough to reliably weaken [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]], [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] performs better with his guaranteed [[Freeze]] ability. Even [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]], who already excels in bursting down Dark enemies, has weaken as a bonus, making it all the more redundant to bring Kotomine & Gilgamesh Cats into Black-centric stages.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Gilgamesh & Kotomine Cats gain a better trait target as well as Zombie Killer, though their preexisting problems remain. They could be used to weaken [[Lord Gravey]] and [[Zir Zeal]], though like previously, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] performs better by weakening [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] on top of [[Slow|slowing]] them. The only advantages Gilgamesh & Kotomine Cats have over Psychocat are slightly better survivability and Area Attack. Even then, Psychocat's superior cooldown is enough to completely replace them.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller}}

